  "lesson": "## A new hook every 8 bars\n\nHot cues on the hooks: B1 and B2 on deck B, A1 on deck A. Every 8 bars, press the next hot cue and snap the crossfader to that deck in the same motion: B1 at bar 9, A1 at bar 17, B2 at bar 25. Each cut is a switch inside 100 ms, on the one.\n\nThis is the hip-hop dropmix from the sources: 8 or 16 bars of each record, cut on the downbeat, no blend. The hot cue press and the crossfader snap are one gesture; the cue press is on the beat and the fader lands on it. Keep both tracks running so the cues retrigger the hook, not the intro.\n",
